@BASE_URL = http://localhost:3333
@url = {{BASE_URL}}/cases
@caseId = 0e3096b4-d87f-4363-812b-51d514a0a81c

# Manual smoke test for case closure lifecycle.
# Preconditions:
# 1. The API is already running at http://localhost:3333; this file does not start containers.
# 2. This file authenticates as the seeded lawyer who manages the selected case.
# 3. Before POST /close, confirm GET /closure returns capabilities.canClose=true.

### Sign in as the seeded case manager
# @name signInAsSeededCaseManager
# @prompt seedPassword Enter HMS_USER_SEED_PASSWORD
POST {{BASE_URL}}/auth/sign-in
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "identifier": "lawyer@hmsadvogados.com.br",
  "password": "{{seedPassword}}"
}

### List cases linked to the signed-in collaborator
# @name listMyCases
GET {{url}}/my
Authorization: Bearer {{signInAsSeededCaseManager.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

# caseId is prefilled with seeded case CASO-20261012-0009, managed by this lawyer.

### Inspect closure state and current blockers
# @name inspectCaseClosure
GET {{url}}/{{caseId}}/closure
Authorization: Bearer {{signInAsSeededCaseManager.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

# Expected: HTTP 200 with legalCase, blockers, events, and capabilities.

### Close the seeded case
POST {{url}}/{{caseId}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{signInAsSeededCaseManager.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "outcome": "agreement",
  "notes": "Closure smoke test with the seeded case manager."
}

# Expected: HTTP 200 with kind "closed"; the selected seeded case has no blockers.
